Spare Kit geometry kernel: notices
==================================

The geometry kernel (projects/engines/geometry) is Spare Kit's own work under the Mozilla Public
License 2.0 (LICENSE at the repository root), except where a file says it is ported from an
outside source. This file holds the licence text of every outside source the kernel takes code
from, and the credit owed to every source the kernel takes code or a method from, as rule 4 of
section 29.20 of the kernel's architecture (chapter 29, sources and licences) requires. It ships
with every binary built from the kernel.

It is generated from the Source: and Consulted: lines of the kernel's crate and module headers and
from the licence texts kept in projects/engines/geometry/notices/, by
`cargo run -p geom-test --bin provenance -- write`; never edit it by hand. CI regenerates it and
fails on any difference.

Each ported source gives its name, how the kernel takes it (section 29.1), its link pinned to a
commit, its licence as the source states it, the kernel files that take from it with the origin
files each comes from and the origin's copyright lines as that file's header copies them, any
further credit, and the licence text in full. Each ported file also starts with its origin files'
notices in full.

The notices of the crates compiled into a shipped binary, such as libm, are not kept here: they
go in the generated third-party notices file (rule 4; build piece G481).


